// CARD a3-01 · SEE: a split-flap calendar over the real Facebook headquarters at 1 Hacker Way, dim; on "three" it flicks month by month from MAR 2015 and locks on MAR 2018: CAMBRIDGE ANALYTICA SUSPENDED · Friday 16 Mar 2018, late evening · SEAM out right
# cine act=fall fx="code:@month_flip;bg:meta_facebook_hq_1_hacker_way;from:2015-03;to:2018-03;go:happened;lab:CAMBRIDGE ANALYTICA SUSPENDED;sub:Friday 16 Mar 2018 · late evening;out:right"
{tense} For three years, nothing happened. Then, on Friday the sixteenth of March, twenty eighteen, Facebook suspended Cambridge Analytica from its platform, late in the **evening**.

// CARD a3-02 · SEE: real printing presses roll, dim; the real Guardian page of 17 March 2018 slides in as a clipping and a red marker underlines its headline · SEAM in right
# cine act=fall fx="code:@clipping_over_footage;clip:stock_news_press_rollers_01;doc:meta_doc_guardian_headline_2018_p1;crop:0,.05,1,.36;mark:.05,.42,.95,.62;go:morning;side:right;in:right"
The next morning, The Observer and The New York Times published within hours of each **other**.
Facebook had suspended Kogan and Wylie too, but the story was already **out**.

// CARD a3-03 · SEE: the real black and white portrait of Christopher Wylie, the camera travelling to his face; on "source" his name card slides in · SEAM out right
# cine act=doubt fx="code:@name_strap;pic:meta_wylie_portrait_bw;go:source;name:CHRISTOPHER WYLIE;role:former director of research, Cambridge Analytica;fx:.5;fy:.35;out:right"
Their source was Christopher Wylie, a former director of research at Cambridge **Analytica**.

// CARD a3-04 · SEE: an empty TV studio, cameras on tripods (no faces); three items land as a list and each is struck on its word: BRIBERY STINGS · HONEY TRAPS · FRONT COMPANIES; CHANNEL 4 NEWS · 19 MAR 2018 · SEAM in right
# cine act=fall fx="code:@roll_call_strike;bg:stock_media_tv_studio_04;names:BRIBERY STINGS~HONEY TRAPS~FRONT COMPANIES;go:bribery;span:1.4;lab:Alexander Nix on Channel 4 News undercover footage · 19 Mar 2018;in:right"
Two days later, Channel 4 News aired undercover footage of the firm's chief executive, Alexander **Nix**.
He talked about bribery stings, honey traps and front companies as possible **services**.

// CARD a3-05 · SEE: the real Centre Point and New Oxford Street; on "suspended" a solid stamp NIX SUSPENDED; on "warrant" WARRANT SOUGHT beside it · SEAM out right
# cine act=fall fx="code:@stamp_dates;pic:meta_new_oxford_street_centrepoint;y:.3;stamps:NIX SUSPENDED^suspended~WARRANT SOUGHT^warrant;gap:20 Mar 2018 · UK data regulator;out:right"
His board suspended him the next **day**. The same day, Britain's data regulator asked a court for a warrant to search the firm's London **offices**.

// CARD a3-06 · SEE: NEW: a desk tear-off calendar, MAR 2018; on "nothing" its pages tear off one a day, 16, 17, 18, 19, 20, the count running to 5 DAYS; it stops on 21, ringed in red: STATEMENT · SEAM in right
# cine act=doubt fx="code:@day_tearoff;bg:meta_zuckerberg_profile_bw;from:16;to:21;month:MAR 2018;go:nothing;span:3;lab:A STATEMENT;sub:of silence;in:right"
Mark Zuckerberg said nothing for five **days**.
Then, on the twenty-first of March, he posted a **statement**.

// CARD a3-07 · SEE: the real Zuckerberg on the F8 2018 stage as a print on the left; his verbatim words to the Senate light up on the right as the voice reads them · SEAM out right · HOLD
# cine act=fall fx="code:@ember_quote;pic:meta_zuckerberg_f8_2018_keynote;q:“It was my mistake, and I'm sorry. I started Facebook, I run it, and I'm responsible for what happens here.”;go:Senate;span:6;name:ZUCKERBERG · 10 APR 2018;src:hearing record · read by a voice actor · photo F8 2018;out:right"
In April, he sat in front of the United States **Senate**, and the next day in front of the **House**.
@zuck: It was my mistake, and I'm sorry. I started Facebook, I run it, and I'm responsible for what happens here.

// CARD a3-08 · SEE: real server racks, dim; HIS OWN DATA WAS SWEPT UP TOO sets low; on "And" a field of gold points pours out from one point: 20,000 SECURITY STAFF · promised by the end of 2018 · SEAM in right
# cine act=doubt fx="code:@dots;bg:meta_noirlab_server_racks;n:12000;go:And;lab:20,000 SECURITY STAFF;sub:promised by the end of 2018;sub2:HIS OWN DATA WAS SWEPT UP TOO;at2:swept;in:right"
He also confirmed that his own data had been swept up with everyone **else's**. (J)
And he promised to grow Facebook's security staff to twenty thousand people by the end of the **year**.

// CARD a3-09 · SEE: the real 43-45 New Oxford Street; on "ceasing" its colour drains, a black border draws round it and CAMBRIDGE ANALYTICA · CEASED OPERATIONS · 2 MAY 2018 types under it · SEAM out right
# cine act=fall fx="code:@mourning_frame;pic:meta_new_oxford_street_43_45;go:ceasing;name:CAMBRIDGE ANALYTICA;date:CLOSED · 2 MAY 2018;fx:.5;fy:.45;out:right"
On the second of May, Cambridge Analytica announced it was ceasing all **operations**.
It blamed a "siege of media coverage" that had driven away almost all of its **customers**.

// CARD a3-10 · SEE: the split-flap calendar returns over a London street: on "gone" it flicks MAR 2018 to MAY 2018 and locks: GONE IN ABOUT SIX WEEKS; then: 2020 · Nix accepts a 7-year director ban · SEAM in right
# cine act=fall fx="code:@month_flip;bg:meta_routemaster_new_oxford;from:2018-03;to:2018-05;go:gone;lab:GONE IN ABOUT SIX WEEKS;sub:2020 · Nix accepts a 7-year director ban;in:right"
The firm that used the data was gone in about six **weeks**.
Two years later, Nix accepted a seven-year ban on running British **companies**.

// CARD a3-11 · SEE: MOTIF: the bill; on "company" it prints CAMBRIDGE ANALYTICA · 2018: CLOSED; THE FIRM IS GONE · the platform is not · SEAM out right
# cine act=lesson fx="code:@bill_tape;bg:meta_el_texture_server_bokeh;lines:NEW MEXICO · 21 OCT 2026^$25,000,000,000~FTC ORDER · 2012^A PROMISE~2015 · DELETION LETTERS^NOT CHECKED~CAMBRIDGE ANALYTICA · 2018^CLOSED;new:3;go:company;lab:THE FIRM IS GONE;sub:the platform is not;out:right"
But the company that gave the data away was just getting **started**.

